<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Democratic Republic of Yemen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1994">1994</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Democratic Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a> was a breakaway state proclaimed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a> on 21 May 1994 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-salim-al-beidh">Ali Salim al-Beidh</a>, the former leader of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-yemen">South Yemen</a>, during the civil war that followed unification. It controlled much of the former south but won no international recognition, and it collapsed when northern forces captured Aden on 7 July 1994.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/democratic-republic-of-yemen.jpg" alt="Democratic Republic of Yemen" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: National Front - الجبهة القومية · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_South_Yemen.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
